  "snippet": "#​499 — November 27, 2026 Read on the Web React Status Ricky Hanlon is Leaving Meta (But Not React) — After years helping get React \"from 4 million to 250 million weekly downloads\", Ricky has left React's birthplace, not...",
  "coverImage": "https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/iyljdqwehjcad5y5dro8.jpg",
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​499 — November 27, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193600/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<div style=\"color: #333;\">\n<div style=\"font-size: 2.7em; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.3em; margin-bottom: 0px;\"> React Status</div>\n</div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193565/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/iyljdqwehjcad5y5dro8.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193565/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"bsky.app\">Ricky Hanlon is Leaving Meta (But Not React)</a></span> — After years helping get React <em>\"from 4 million to 250 million weekly downloads\"</em>, Ricky has left React's birthplace, noting <em>\"most of the React Core team have left Meta\"</em>. This is more an 'end of an era' than big news, as he'll continue to work on React, and <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193566/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">React getting its own foundation</a> this year showed us the direction of travel.</p>\n<p>Ricky Hanlon </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 Paul O'Shannessy, who pushed React's first public code in 2013 and helped form the foundation, also left Meta this year and wrote <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193567/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">a look back at his 14 years there</a>.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193564/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"113\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/cba882ff.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193564/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"fandf.co\">Build Durable AI Agents &amp; Workflows in TypeScript</a></span> — Trigger.dev runs AI agents as tasks inside your codebase, in plain TypeScript with full control of runtime. No serverless timeouts, so even long agents run to completion, surviving refreshes, redeploys, and crashes. Write your logic, test it, and deploy agents that scale on demand.</p>\n<p>Trigger.dev <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193568/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">The Roadmap to TanStack Query v6</a></span> — Dominik has shared the plan for TanStack Query's next major version, and it's focused on cleaning up, going ESM-only, React 19 as a baseline, etc. In his words, <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193569/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><em>\"we'll break things, but not too many.\"</em></a> If you've got things to say, feedback is welcomed.</p>\n<p>Dominik Dorfmeister </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193570/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.zachleat.com\">Your Tools are Hiding npm Audits From You</a></span> — <code>npm audit</code> on a new <code>create-next-app</code> app shows '0 vulnerabilities' but Next vendors over 100 packages and the audit doesn't notice those. To help counter this, Zach has built the <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193571/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">📊 Prototype Pollution Report</a> which compares numerous frameworks' behaviors and vendored dependency vulnerabilities.</p>\n<p>Zach Leatherman </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193572/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.gmoniava.com\">React Forms Beyond <code>onSubmit</code></a></span> — See the differences between a form built three ways (with <code>onSubmit</code>, React 19's <code>action</code> prop, and <code>onSubmit</code> plus <code>useTransition</code>). Each has pros and cons, shown in a comparison table.</p>\n<p>Giorgi Moniava </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193573/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Can You Confidently Ship to Production From Your Phone?</a> – How an Expo engineer fixed a bug and shipped an over-the-air update while on a walk. <cite>Rami Maalouf (Expo)</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193574/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Why Base44 Now Generates New Apps with TanStack Start</a> – Bye to SPAs plus separate backend functions; hello full-stack apps. <cite>Netanel Gilad (Base44)</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193575/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Building Bulletproof React Components</a> – A re-run of a classic from the co-creator of <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193576/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">SWR</a>. <cite>Shu Ding</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193577/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React Testing Library is Faster When It's Part of the DOM</a> – An interesting approach. <cite>Scott Cooper</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>🛠  Code, Tools &amp; Libraries</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193578/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/zlcmbt26ptp7pwht5tzb.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193578/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"generativeloaders.com\">Generative Loaders: Loading States for Generative UI</a></span> — Almost fifty elegant and accessible ways to show the 'thinking' moments in UIs, like when an LLM is generating text, an image is being generated, or even just while a background process is working on something.</p>\n<p>Kasturi Khanke </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><span>🔊</span> <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193579/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"buttons.joshwcomeau.com\">Button Sounds: Tactile Click Sounds for Your UI</a></span> — Popular dev blogger Josh (who I've just learnt has a background in audio) recorded numerous clicks and toggle sounds for us to use. There's a <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193580/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><code>useButtonSounds</code> hook</a>, and the site lets you quickly check them all out.</p>\n<p>Josh W. Comeau </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193581/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"vcarl.com\">Sashay: Sliding, Resizable Panes for React</a></span> — A way to let users arrange your app the way they want by dragging and snapping edges between panes (and on phones, the edges become tabs). The homepage is a good demo itself.</p>\n<p>Carl Vitullo </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193582/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">Exact: Expo's Experimental All-Platform App Framework</a></span> — It's not React, but it's interesting to see the company behind so much React Native tooling building a Rust-powered multi-platform app framework. A big focus is on being 'agent native'.</p>\n<p>Expo </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193583/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">File Viewer: A Browser-Native File Viewer for Internal Apps</a></span> — Provides read-only views for Office, PDF/OFD, CAD files, archives, email and similar tricky formats, with integrations for React, Vue, and Svelte. The <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193584/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">docs site</a> has demos you can try out along with info on all the supported formats.</p>\n<p>Flyfish Dev </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193585/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">react-pdf 11.1</a> – Display PDFs in your React app. Now on a newer version of <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193586/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">PDF.js</a> with better performance and text selecting. (<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193587/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Homepage with live demo</a>.)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193588/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">jest-dom 8.0</a> – Custom DOM matchers for Jest and Vitest. Note that Vitest users now need Vitest 5 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193589/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Voltra 2.7</a> – A way to build iOS <em>Live Activities</em> and widgets as React Native components.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>📊 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193590/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">echarts-for-react 3.1</a> – React wrapper for Apache ECharts.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193591/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Material UI 9.6</a> – Comprehensive React component suite.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>⚛️ Inconsistent code from AI agents? <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193592/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Nexity</a> pairs rules in plain files with 8 reviewers and auditors. For Claude Code, Codex, Cursor. MIT.</p>\n<p>📱 Ship React Native fixes without waiting on app review. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193593/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Get Bitrise’s free guide to safe OTA updates</a>.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📢  Elsewhere in the ecosystem</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>🤖 Vercel's <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193594/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">eve</a>, a Next.js-style framework for building AI agents, <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193595/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">has reached its 1.0 release</a>. It's <em>not</em> a React project, but includes integrations for Next.js and TanStack Start, plus React bindings for building your own agent UIs.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>If you're chasing bugs through a production bundle, <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193596/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Chrome's DevTools can now show original variable and function names</a> in scopes/stack traces/console (as long as the source maps follow <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193597/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">the 'scopes' proposal</a>).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🗳️ <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193598/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\"><em>The State of JavaScript 2026</em> survey</a> closes soon, so it's worth taking if you haven't yet as it's also a good way to put newer techniques on your radar.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🎉 The Svelte team is <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193599/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">celebrating the project's tenth birthday</a>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
  "attachments": []
}